  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Express the following as a single fraction.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{3}{x^2}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{4x+3}{x^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{3}{x^2}&=\\frac{4x}{x^2}+\\frac{3}{x^2}\\\\\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{3}{x^2}&=\\frac{4x+3}{x^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{5}{x+1}-\\frac{2}{(x+1)(x+2)}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{5x+8}{(x+1)(x+2)}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{x+1}-\\frac{2}{(x+1)(x+2)}&=\\frac{5(x+2)-2}{(x+1)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{5}{x+1}-\\frac{2}{(x+1)(x+2)}&=\\frac{5x+8}{(x+1)(x+2)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{x+2}{x^2-9}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3x-4}{(x-3)(x+3)}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{x+2}{x^2-9}&=\\frac{2(x-3)+(x+2)}{(x-3)(x+3)}\\\\\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{x+2}{x^2-9}&=\\frac{2x-6+x+2}{(x-3)(x+3)}\\\\\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{x+2}{x^2-9}&=\\frac{3x-4}{(x-3)(x+3)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{3}{x(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{x(x+1)}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{5x+1}{x(x-1)(x+1)}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{x(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{x(x+1)}&=\\frac{3(x+1)+2(x-1)}{x(x-1)(x+1)}\\\\\\frac{3}{x(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{x(x+1)}&=\\frac{3x+3+2x-2}{x(x-1)(x+1)}\\\\\\frac{3}{x(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{x(x+1)}&=\\frac{5x+1}{x(x-1)(x+1)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{4}{x^2+4x+4}-\\frac{2}{x^2+x-2}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{2(x-4)}{(x-1)(x+2)^2}$\n\nFactorise the denominators, then use their lowest common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+4x+4&=(x+2)^2\\\\x^2+x-2&=(x+2)(x-1)\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4}{x^2+4x+4}-\\frac{2}{x^2+x-2}&=\\frac{4(x-1)-2(x+2)}{(x-1)(x+2)^2}\\\\\\frac{4}{x^2+4x+4}-\\frac{2}{x^2+x-2}&=\\frac{2x-8}{(x-1)(x+2)^2}\\\\\\frac{4}{x^2+4x+4}-\\frac{2}{x^2+x-2}&=\\frac{2(x-4)}{(x-1)(x+2)^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{3}{x^2-x-6}+\\frac{4}{x^2-4x+3}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{7x+5}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+2)}$\n\nFactorise the denominators, then use their lowest common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-x-6&=(x-3)(x+2)\\\\x^2-4x+3&=(x-3)(x-1)\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{x^2-x-6}+\\frac{4}{x^2-4x+3}&=\\frac{3(x-1)+4(x+2)}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{3}{x^2-x-6}+\\frac{4}{x^2-4x+3}&=\\frac{3x-3+4x+8}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{3}{x^2-x-6}+\\frac{4}{x^2-4x+3}&=\\frac{7x+5}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+2)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{x}{2-x}+\\frac{2}{x^2-4}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{2-2x-x^2}{(x-2)(x+2)}$\n\nUse $2-x=-(x-2)$ before combining the fractions.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{2-x}+\\frac{2}{x^2-4}&=-\\frac{x}{x-2}+\\frac{2}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{x}{2-x}+\\frac{2}{x^2-4}&=\\frac{-x(x+2)+2}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{x}{2-x}+\\frac{2}{x^2-4}&=\\frac{2-2x-x^2}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{3}{x^2-1}-\\frac{2}{1-x}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{2x+5}{(x-1)(x+1)}$\n\nUse $1-x=-(x-1)$, so subtracting the second fraction becomes addition.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{x^2-1}-\\frac{2}{1-x}&=\\frac{3}{(x-1)(x+1)}+\\frac{2}{x-1}\\\\\\frac{3}{x^2-1}-\\frac{2}{1-x}&=\\frac{3+2(x+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\\\\\frac{3}{x^2-1}-\\frac{2}{1-x}&=\\frac{2x+5}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
